<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/commercial-roof.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/commercial-roof-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/commercial-roof.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="768" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.15"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/what-we-handle/">Services</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Commercial &amp; HOA Claim Appraisal</span></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Commercial and HOA Claim Appraisal in Kansas</h1><p class="lede">A hailstorm that crosses a Wichita business park or a Johnson County townhome community can produce a seven-figure disagreement. We value large, multi-building losses with the documentation a panel expects.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line" href="/request-kansas-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Properties</dt><dd>Commercial, HOA, multifamily</dd></div><div><dt>Roof types</dt><dd>TPO, EPDM, metal, mod-bit</dd></div><div><dt>Scale</dt><dd>Single site to portfolio</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>Why commercial claims stall</h2>
<p>Commercial property disputes are rarely about whether a storm happened. They are about how many square feet of membrane are damaged, whether a standing-seam metal roof with dents is “functionally” damaged, how a coinsurance clause applies, and whether business interruption figures line up with the building repair timeline. Each of those questions has a dollar answer, which makes many of them a fit for appraisal.</p>
<h2>What we value</h2>
<ul>
<li>Single-ply, modified bitumen, built-up and metal roof systems, including tapered insulation and drains.</li>
<li>Rooftop HVAC units, condenser coils, skylights and parapet metal.</li>
<li>Exterior finishes such as EIFS, metal panels, brick and storefront glazing.</li>
<li>Interior build-outs damaged by water intrusion after a roof failure.</li>
<li>Multi-building HOA communities where each building must be scoped on its own.</li>
</ul>
<h2>HOA boards and property managers</h2>
<p>Townhome and condo associations in Overland Park, Olathe, Lenexa and east Wichita often face the same question after a storm: replace every roof in the community, or only the buildings the carrier approved? We document building by building so the board can make decisions on facts and the panel can see the pattern across the whole community.</p>
<h2>Churches, schools and agricultural businesses</h2>
<p>Kansas has thousands of metal-roofed churches, grain operations and shop buildings that sit in hail country. We value metal panels, trim, gutters and fasteners with the same rigor as a shingle roof, and we account for the access and equipment large buildings require.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Illustrative example only</b>On a hypothetical 40-unit townhome community, a carrier approving 12 roofs instead of 40 creates a gap that can exceed several hundred thousand dollars. That is the kind of dispute where documentation per building matters most.</div>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary><span>Can appraisal resolve a coinsurance penalty?</span><svg class="pl" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Appraisal can establish values that feed the coinsurance calculation, such as replacement cost. Whether the penalty applies is often a coverage question.</p></div></details><details><summary><span>Do you handle business interruption?</span><svg class="pl" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>We focus on property damage valuation and work alongside forensic accountants when business income is part of the dispute.</p></div></details><details><summary><span>How do you price large roofs?</span><svg class="pl" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>From measured quantities, manufacturer specifications and current material and labor pricing, including equipment and access for the specific building.</p></div></details></div>
